These eight WAV files are PLACEHOLDERS. They are synthetic tone bursts, not
speech, and nobody said the sentences in transcripts.tsv.

They exist so the harness can be run end to end today: eight languages, a file
per language, a reference per file, a silence-trimmable energy contour and a
pause between two bursts where the product vocabulary belongs. Every code path
from `--corpus` through normalisation to the printed tables is exercised by
them.

What they are not is evidence. `docs/features/voice/plans/ENGINE_BENCHMARK.md` already
says the smoke fixture proves the harness runs and that no number derived from
it appears in a decision table; with placeholder audio that is doubly true, and
the harness prints `smoke fixture: PLACEHOLDER` in its run header for as long as
this file is here.

Replacing them is `docs/features/voice/archive/QUESTIONS.md` Q-V2: eight recordings, by
native or fluent speakers, of the sentence in transcripts.tsv followed by a
pause and then the seven product names. 16 kHz, mono, 16-bit PCM WAV, 3-5
seconds. Delete this file in the same change - the header line is what tells a
reader whether the fixture they are looking at is real.
